From: Azimjon Ulmasov <azimjon.ulmasov@chainguard.dev>
Date: Thu, 9 Oct 2026 15:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: skip tls-basic-anon when OpenSSL has no anonymous ciphers

The test already skips when OpenSSL reports "no shared cipher", but it
greps the sender output for the message prefix "Errorstack:" that
librelp no longer emits (src/tcp.c prints "OpenSSL Error Stack:"), and
the error is reported by the receiver. OpenSSL 4.0 removed the anonymous
cipher suites, so look for the message in the receiver error log.

The receiver error log is kept under the per-test ${TESTDIR}
(lrtb_<port>/) rather than the shared error.out.log in tests/: under a
parallel "make check" other tests also write error.out.log and their
cleanup removes error.*.log, so the skip check could miss the message
or find no file at all. This follows upstream commit c0bb2f0 ("tests:
isolate certvalid untrusted error log").
---
--- a/tests/tls-basic-anon.sh
+++ b/tests/tls-basic-anon.sh
@@ -2,14 +2,15 @@
 . ${srcdir:=$(pwd)}/test-framework.sh
 
 function actual_test() {
-	startup_receiver -l $TEST_TLS_LIB -T -e error.out.log
+	local errorlog="${TESTDIR}/error.out.log"
+	startup_receiver -l $TEST_TLS_LIB -T -e "$errorlog"
 
 	echo 'Send Message...'
 	./send -l $TEST_TLS_LIB -t 127.0.0.1 -p $TESTPORT -m "testmessage" -T $OPT_VERBOSE 1>>${OUTFILE} 2>&1
 
-	# "relpTcpLastSSLErrorMsg: Errorstack: error:1417A0C1:SSL routines:tls_post_process_client_hello:no shared cipher"
+	# "relpTcpLastSSLErrorMsg: OpenSSL Error Stack: error:0A0000C1:SSL routines::no shared cipher"
 	stop_receiver
-	if check_output_only "relpTcpLastSSLErrorMsg\: Errorstack\: error\:.*\:no shared cipher"; then
+	if check_output_only "relpTcpLastSSLErrorMsg\: .*error\:.*\:no shared cipher" "$errorlog"; then
 		printf "\nSKIP: openssl reported 'no shared cipher'\n"
 		printf "\nDEBUG: content of ${OUTFILE}\n"
 		cat $FILE_TO_CHECK
